#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:5
#: dca0f2b902a6424a9fd947eb67accca5
msgid "Traditional Helicopter – Tailrotor Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:7
#: 382a0f3de3ec446dbfb686aa09a4696a
msgid ""
"There are several ways for controlling the tailrotor to maintain yaw "
"stabilization and provide yaw control, and each have a unique setup.  The"
" :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` parameter is used to specify method for"
" controlling the tailrotor.  A list of available tail types is given "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:9
#: edc10aa43c27489dade245c61c9207fa
msgid ""
"Servo Only: ArduPilot will supply the tail rotor stabilization like a "
"tail rotor gyro and control the pitch of the tail rotor blades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:10
#: 94d7dfede2954d3381d5eda60e8dfb86
msgid ""
"Servo with External Gyro: ArduPilot will output yaw demands without "
"direct yaw attitude stabilization which is provided via an external gyro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:11
#: df044e5b6672465988d599e40ed8b1c4
msgid ""
"Direct Drive Variable Pitch (DDVP): Instead of the tail rotor being "
"driven from the main rotor via mechanical coupling as in the above cases,"
" an electric motor is used with motor controlled(ramp up/down, operating "
"point) by ArduPilot. Main yaw control is via tail blade pitch servo, as "
"above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:12
#: ecfa8f64360d48ebb9ac52fb1af835a8
msgid ""
"Direct Drive Fixed Pitch Clockwise (DDFP CW): Tail rotor is driven by a "
"motor whose ESC is controlled by ArduPilot to maintain yaw stability and "
"yaw direction. Used with clockwise rotating main rotors, when viewed from"
" above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:13
#: 83984095b7404c3eb66db92e14653482
msgid ""
"Direct Drive Fixed Pitch Counter-Clockwise (DDFP CCW): Tail rotor driven "
"by a motor whose ESC is controlled by ArudPilot to maintain yaw stability"
" and yaw direction. Used with counter-clockwise rotating main rotors, "
"when viewed from above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:17
#: 76d6be0afa784b9f969da8080b12ff99
msgid "Tailrotor Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:20
#: f6cac557d86f449cb22df984a7052b16
msgid "Servo Only :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:22
#: 02835a1c79734ff49304e5bc33d0d677
msgid ""
"The Servo Only tail type uses a servo connected to an autopilot output "
"whose ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` is selected as ``Motor4`` to control the "
"tailrotor pitch slider.  The tailrotor speed is controlled by a physical "
"connection (tailrotor shaft or belt) to the engine and main shaft. "
"Depending on your servo setup and mechanical throws, set the "
"``SERVOx_MIN``, ``SERVOx_MAX``, and ``SERVOx_REVERSED`` parameter values."
"  Setting the ``SERVOx_TRIM`` is discussed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:24
#: d7bb636e087a4c618c0a52b01d952834
msgid ""
"Be sure to check the direction of operation of the Tail Servo. Move the "
"rudder stick and notice the change in tail rotor pitch. Be sure that its "
"increase or decrease of pitch is such that the change in thrust will "
"result in the desired direction of movement. If not, reverse the servo "
"direction with the ``SERVOx_REVERSED`` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:27
#: e40ab2fdc15440e0b5fc9ba67970c942
msgid "Servo with External Gyro :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:29
#: 3224d38e377c43dca81be7c55478aa14
msgid ""
"Instead of ArduPilot controlling both the desired yaw rate and stability,"
" this option relies on an external gyro for stabilization. A servo is "
"still used to input yaw rate demands to the tail and its setup as above, "
"for the Servo Only case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:31
#: 0a5a32a83ba5429a99f0d3c1e24fefca
msgid ""
"The external gyro gain can be set by the :ref:`H_GYR_GAIN<H_GYR_GAIN>` "
"parameter using the autopilot's \"Motor7\" output "
"function,``SERVOx_FUNCTION``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:33
#: 9ab9f324f4584fc99d30499f17bd1829
msgid ""
"In ACRO mode, this gain can be changed to the value of the "
":ref:`H_GYR_GAIN_ACRO<H_GYR_GAIN_ACRO>` parameter, if non-zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:36
#: 0cc3492560b54cb8a251f3ee860ab9c5
msgid "Direct Drive Variable Pitch :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` = 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:38
#: eeeadca0c3f84901a31cf245756e3636
msgid ""
"The Direct Drive Variable Pitch (DDVP) tail type uses a separate tail "
"motor with a variable pitch propeller.  A separate servo is used to "
"control the tailrotor pitch.  The setup of the servo is similar to the "
"servo only tail type. ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` \"Motor4\" is assigned to the "
"output number that corresponds to the servo channel the tailrotor servo "
"is physically connected (defaults to output 4).  For the tail motor, the "
"\"HeliTailRSC\" (\"32\") is assigned to the motor/servo channel to which "
"the tail motor ESC is physically connected (defaults to output 7)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:40
#: 9837c892b4e84177b2e466a26580c03b
msgid ""
"The range of the motor ESC is controlled by its output's "
"``SERVOx_MIN/MAX`` parameters and ArduPilot will ramp it output up or "
"down, as appropriate, to its normal operating value set by the "
":ref:`H_TAIL_SPEED<H_TAIL_SPEED>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:43
#: 6e43ee5013044ee2af37018cbcc33542
msgid "Direct Drive Fixed Pitch :ref:`H_TAIL_TYPE <H_TAIL_TYPE>` = 3 or 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:45
#: 68fb800655554f60b0b2ea71736b9489
msgid ""
"The Direct Drive Fixed Pitch (DDFP) tail type uses a fixed pitch tail "
"rotor and separate motor. The stabilization and yaw is controlled by the "
"speed of this motor. It has two options: one where the main rotor rotates"
" clockwise when viewed from above and the other where the main rotor "
"rotates counter-clockwise when viewed from above.  Be sure to select the "
"DDFP tail type for the main rotor rotation.  In this case, the control of"
" tailrotor thrust is accomplished through tailrotor speed since it is a "
"fixed pitch propeller. The ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` of \"36\" (Motor4) should "
"be assigned to the servo channel to which the tailrotor ESC is physically"
" connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:47
#: 2f4d6c82cb7a43f681f925d1cdbe0443
msgid ""
"There are several parameters that provide the ability to linearize the "
"thrust produced by the tail rotor motor and therefore provide better "
"control:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:49
#: 0f851aa592da4334bf6aaab4c848cfbe
msgid ""
":ref:`H_DDFP_THST_EXPO<H_DDFP_THST_EXPO>` - Tail rotor DDFP motor thrust "
"curve exponent (0.0 for linear to 1.0 for second order curve). Default = "
"0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:50
#: 1830c70fa8aa41e494ccd5c6c574b846
msgid ""
":ref:`H_DDFP_SPIN_MIN<H_DDFP_SPIN_MIN>` - Point at which the DDFP motor "
"thrust starts expressed as a number from 0 to 1 in the entire output "
"range.  Default = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:51
#: ecfff61f60594489af1c8e26cbdd941f
msgid ""
":ref:`H_DDFP_SPIN_MAX<H_DDFP_SPIN_MAX>` - Point at which the DDFP motor "
"thrust saturates expressed as a number from 0 to 1 in the entire output "
"range. Default = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:52
#: 289b39b1158747a1998aa9407064b026
msgid ""
":ref:`H_DDFP_BAT_IDX<H_DDFP_BAT_IDX>` - Index of battery to be used for "
"voltage compensation. Default = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:53
#: 194c3f5cc9424bdab6ea8e8fb3bb3b96
msgid ""
":ref:`H_DDFP_BAT_V_MAX<H_DDFP_BAT_V_MAX>` - Battery voltage compensation "
"maximum voltage (voltage above this will have no additional scaling "
"effect on thrust). Recommend 4.2 * cell count, 0 = Disabled. Default = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:54
#: 54286e4698f14457bc3b235c8f7bbdfd
msgid ""
":ref:`H_DDFP_BAT_V_MIN<H_DDFP_BAT_V_MIN>` - Battery voltage compensation "
"minimum voltage (voltage below this will have no additional scaling "
"effect on thrust). Recommend 3.3 * cell count, 0 = Disabled. Default = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:56
#: 83f8aeed538f4d24a0c6b37f411a8e3c
msgid ""
"These parameters should be set similarly to how Copter's motor scaling "
"parameterss are setup. See :ref:`Copters Motor Thrust Scaling <motor-"
"thrust-scaling>` document for more information."
msgstr ""

