#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:71
#: 0d7fc6cc119e4989bb6104645d22cb11
msgid "Setting Tail Trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:73
#: 09170c1ec61e4a52a5c12caed4139906
msgid ""
"Setting the trim value of the Servo output is important to ensuring that "
"the integrator offset of the tail rotor control loop is minimized, to "
"maximize control range.  Collective to tailrotor compensation can also "
"help with this and is discussed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:76
#: 07dae284f16445f2befdf0fa2d1d5352
msgid "For DDFP tails using V4.5 or later"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:78
#: 3aae08db96744e5693b660922e320128
msgid ""
"If no :ref:`collective-to-tailrotor-compensation` is used, then it is "
"recommended that the :ref:`H_YAW_TRIM<H_YAW_TRIM>` parameter is set to "
"minimize the yaw I term in the hover.  To determine this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:80
#: 096fea3742e84f528cb66c89294f0f57
msgid ""
"Ensure PID logging is switched on in the :ref:`LOG_BITMASK<LOG_BITMASK>` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:81
#: 2178c8b39be84dd6a6767381838c079a
msgid ""
"Hover the aircraft, maintaining altitude.  For best results, this is "
"preferentially done on a light wind day. If possible, leave the aircraft "
"drift with the wind and mintain a fixed height (ALT HOLD is very useful "
"for this)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:82
#: a74227a34252445c9072ada4e2ef7b6a
msgid ""
"After the flight, download the log and find the ``PIDY.I`` message.  Zoom"
" in the on that portion of the flight with the hovering (should be a "
"relatively flat line). Determine the average value of the I term. Enter "
"this average value in the :ref:`H_YAW_TRIM<H_YAW_TRIM>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:83
#: 842334ee0ef64941924660c1234fee0b
msgid ""
"To confirm this has been done correctly repeat the flight.  Now, in the "
"hovering portion of the flight, the yaw I Term should be close to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:85
#: a11f18af1cd246c082e7ed27e5165c3d
msgid ""
"If :ref:`collective-to-tailrotor-compensation` is used, then set the "
":ref:`H_YAW_TRIM<H_YAW_TRIM>` sufficient to compensate for the main rotor"
" zero blade pitch drag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:88
#: 45f48774af6c4182a91b5ab3141fb5e2
msgid "Other Tail Types and DDFP using firmware before V4.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:90
#: a5c11a7bbd1545d3a53e4c9b9c9cbe96
msgid ""
"If no :ref:`collective-to-tailrotor-compensation` is used,  then it is "
"recommended that the ``SERVOx_TRIM`` for the tailrotor servo is set to "
"the PWM that corresponds to the tailrotor pitch required for hover, or "
"the motor speed for DDFP. To determine this, hover the aircraft.  After "
"the flight, pull the log and determine the average PWM value for the "
"servo for hovering flight.  Either set that as the ``SERVOx_TRIM`` or "
"mechanically adjust the tail pitch (non-DDFP tail types) for the tail "
"pitch corresponding to the PWM.  Then set the ``SERVOx_TRIM`` to the "
"servo midpoint. The latter approach is usually preferable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:92
#: 0ec845981a1443528422b7654338a57b
msgid ""
"If If no :ref:`collective-to-tailrotor-compensation` is used,  the set "
"the ``SERVOx_TRIM`` for the PWM that corresponds to zero tailrotor pitch."
"  Or, the tailrotor pitch can be mechanically adjusted to zero pitch for "
"the servo midpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:97
#: 86ee7c6343424b2eb8f12359f08c2802
msgid "Collective to Tailrotor Compensation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:99
#: ac3dda4dd97f40c280d955d8cdd9ae71
msgid ""
"Collective to tailrotor compensation is used to remove the effects of the"
" aircraft momentarily yawing when the collective pitch is changed rapidly"
" and to minimize integrator offsets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tailrotor-setup.rst:101
#: 841a1c165bd049639c5b990d38df5930
msgid ""
"The parameter :ref:`H_COL2YAW<H_COL2YAW>` is used to set the compensation"
" gain.  This implementation uses an accepted helicopter performance "
"relationship between helicopter power required and weight.  Setting this "
"parameter will only be valid for one rotor speed.  Set the tailrotor "
"pitch so it is zero deg blade pitch at the ``SERVOx_TRIM`` value. If the "
"rotor speed is changed then the parameter might require retuning.  The "
"relationship uses collective to the 1.5 power to determine the tailrotor "
"correction.  It is recommended to start at 0.5 and increase the parameter"
" until there is little to no yawing when changing the collective pitch.  "
"One other way would be to determine the yaw required for hovering as well"
" as the collective and then calculate the value."
msgstr ""

